**Package:** exllamav3 v0.0.30+cu128.torch2.10.0

**Dependencies:**
- torch >= 2.6.0
- flash-attn >= 2.7.4.post1
- tokenizers >= 0.21.1
- numpy >= 2.1.0
- rich
- typing-extensions
- ninja
- safetensors >= 0.3.2
- pyyaml
- marisa-trie
- kbnf >= 0.4.2
- formatron >= 0.5.0
- pydantic == 2.11.0
- xformers

**Main contents:**
- `exllamav3_ext.cpython-313-x86_64-linux-gnu.so` (551 MB compiled extension)
- `exllamav3/` Python package with:
  - `architecture/` — model support for: apertus, arcee, cohere, cohere2, decilm, dots1, ernie4_5, ernie4_5_moe, exaone4, gemma2, gemma3, gemma4, glm4, glm4_moe, glm4v, glm4v_moe, hcxvisionv2, hyperclovax, iquestcoder, llama, mimo, minimax_m2, ministral3, mistral, mistral3, mixtral, nanochat, olmo3, olmohybrid, phi3, qwen2, qwen2_5_vl, qwen3, qwen3_5, qwen3_moe, qwen3_next, qwen3_vl, qwen3_vl_moe, seedoss, smollm3, solar_open_moe, step3_5
  - `cache/` — KV cache management (fp16, quant, recurrent)
  - `conversion/` — model conversion, quantization, calibration
  - CUDA kernels (attention, activation, norm, GEMM, etc.)
